# Phase 59: Nucleus Daemon (Unified Runtime)
**Goal:** Implement the "Presence-Aware" Daemon as a parallel service.
**Strategy:** Non-Destructive Additive Build.

## 1. Core Infrastructure (Additive)
*   [ ] **Module:** Create `mcp_server_nucleus/daemon/` package.
*   [ ] **Entry Point:** Create `scripts/nucleus_daemon.py` (New CLI).
*   [ ] **Service Class:** Implement `NucleusDaemon` with `asyncio` loop.

## 2. Presence Monitor (The Sensor)
*   [ ] **Logic:** Implement `PresenceMonitor` class.
    *   **Check 1:** `last_interaction` timestamp from `events.jsonl` (tail).
    *   **Check 2:** VS Code Process detection (using `psutil` or similar if available, else fallback to file system mtime).
*   [ ] **State:** Maintain `UserStatus` (ONLINE/OFFLINE).

## 3. Internal Orchestrator (The Runtime)
*   [ ] **Integration:** Import [SwarmsOrchestrator](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/runtime/orchestrator.py#8-157) into the Daemon.
*   [ ] **Trigger:** When `UserStatus` switches to OFFLINE (> 5 mins), trigger `orchestrator.run_maintenance_loop()`.
    *   *Note:* This replaces the logic of [autopilot_v2.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/scripts/autopilot_v2.py) but runs smartly.

## 4. Verification (The Proof)
*   [ ] **Simulated Test:** `python scripts/verify_daemon.py`.
    *   Mock "User Active" -> Daemon Sleeps.
    *   Mock "User Offline" -> Daemon Wakes.

## 5. Safety
*   [ ] **Isolation:** The Daemon will use a separate log file `daemon.log`.
*   [ ] **No Conflict:** It will respect the [state.json](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/autonomous_state.json) locking mechanism (Atomic Claims) so it plays nice with any manual scripts running.
